                <div class="pa-callout__content">
                    <h4 class="pa-callout__heading">Experimental</h4>
                    <p><code>pa-sections</code> and the stepper it drives (<code>pa-steps</code>) are in core as <strong>experimental</strong> components (<code>_sections.scss</code>, <code>_steps.scss</code>, <code>js/sections.js</code>). <strong>Class names, modifiers and markup may still change</strong> — pin an exact version if you build on them. Sticky layouts work inside the app shell automatically: <code>js/sections.js</code> marks the content wrapper with <code>pa-sections-host</code> while a block is on the page.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p><code>pa-sections</code> is one long piece of content split into sections — a EULA, a form, a settings page — plus a navigator (<code>pa-steps</code>) that the block <strong>controls</strong>: it marks the section you are in, ticks off what you have read or filled in, colours steps by the state of their fields, and jumps to a section on click. Sections are <strong>plain by default</strong> (one continuous document on the page background); <code>--boxed</code> puts the whole document in one box, <code>--cards</code> boxes each section.</p>

